enu - Image - Research The #7 undergraduate university in Canada for sponsored research funding ( 2025 Maclean's University Rankings ). Apply How to Apply Tuition and Fees Admission Requirements Scholarships, Awards, and Financial Aid Career Development Follow our five-step application process and start your UPEI journey today! About Us About UPEI History and Mission Governance Explore the Campus Careers at UPEI Mega Menu - Image - About Us UPEI continues to excel in student enrolment, research, and faculty awards. × search Custom Search Sort by Relevance Date UPEI Human Resources Breadcrumb Home UPEI Human Resources UPEI Human Resources Human Resources seeks to deliver progressive, best-practice HR services to provide opportunities and information to UPEI employees and the general public. The Human Resources department at UPEI supports over 1,250 faculty, staff, and students. As a member of the UPEI team, you'll have access to vibrant student programs, world-class research opportunities, state-of-the-art facilities, and innovative collaborations. Are you ready to apply? It's easy! Create a UPEI account Complete the UPEI application Submit your completed UPEI application and fee Start your UPEI application Academic Positions Sessional Positions Staff Positions Student Positions Guide for New Islanders UPEI's main campus is located in Charlottetown, PEI's capital city. Historic streetscapes, parks, and buildings; and shops, restaurants, pubs, theatres, and art galleries provide a comfortable setting for Prince Edward Island's only university. Prince Edward Island is rich in history, culture, and a quality of life that is second to none. Located in the Gulf of St. Lawrence on Canada's east coast, \"The Island\" is famous for its beautiful beaches, pastoral landscape, and a dynamic cultural scene. Join us today! Contact Human Resources Department University of Prince Edward Island 902-566-0514 For general inquiries, please email us at hrgeneral@upei.ca . For anything else, please go to our contacts page . Relevant Links About UPEI Resources for Faculty and Staff About UPEI UPEI Human Resources Employment Opportunities Open Competitions Closed Competitions Senior Academic and Administrative Positions Director of Integrated Data Analysis Interim Vice-President, Academic and Research A Guide for New Islanders Contacts Resources for Faculty and Staff Resources for Retirees Collective Agreements Resources for Student Employees Pension Plan for the Employees of the University of Prince Edward Island UPEI Labour Relations Health, Safety, and Environment Staff Relevant Links About UPEI Resources for Faculty and Staff Join the UPEI team today! View all jobs at UPEI Events and Social What's Happening at UPEI? Sep 2 Bachelor of Education Information Session 6:30pm Sep 3 Welcome Week: Grad Student Mixer, hosted by the Faculty of Graduate Studies 4:30pm\n  W.A. Murphy Student Centre Sep 4 Welcome Week: Residence Move-in and Welcome Week Check-in 9:00am\n  Performing Arts Centre and Residence Sep 4 Welcome Week: The UPEI Experience Presentation 11:00am\n  Bill and Denise Andrew Hall See All Events Have a question? Contact studentsupport@upei.ca UPEI Human Resources Full Site Employment Opportunities » Open Competitions » Closed Competitions ▼ Senior Academic and Administrative Positions » Director of Integrated Data Analysis » Interim Vice-President, Academic and Research ▼ A Guide for New Islanders Contacts Resources for Faculty and Staff » Resources for Retirees » Collective Agreements ▼ Resources for Student Employees Pension Plan for the Employees of the University of Prince Edward Island UPEI Labour Relations Health, Safety, and Environment Staff 550 University Ave, Charlottetown Prince Edward Island, Canada C1A 4P3 Quick Links Academic Calendar MyUPEI | Campus Login Bookstore Staff and Faculty Lookup Study Abroad Library Explore the Campus Crisis Centre Athletics and Recreation Moodle Research Faculties and Schools Conference Services Health and Wellness Sexual Violence Prevention and Response Office The University of Prince Edward Island recognizes and acknowledges our location in the unceded, traditional territory of the Mi’kmaq People of PEI. Connect with UPEI Copyright © 2026  University of Prince Edward Island. All Rights Reserved | Disclaimer | Privacy Policy | UPEI SAFE | Website Edits Our website uses cookies to provide the best browsing experience. By using this site or closing this message, you agree to our Disclaimer and Web Privacy Statement . Read Disclaimer OK No, thanks"
