ols Key Research Dates Robertson Library Mega Menu - Image - Research The #7 undergraduate university in Canada for sponsored research funding ( 2025 Maclean's University Rankings ). Apply How to Apply Tuition and Fees Admission Requirements Scholarships, Awards, and Financial Aid Career Development Follow our five-step application process and start your UPEI journey today! About Us About UPEI History and Mission Governance Explore the Campus Careers at UPEI Mega Menu - Image - About Us UPEI continues to excel in student enrolment, research, and faculty awards. × search Custom Search Sort by Relevance Date Lecturer - Three-Year Term Position - Department of Biomedical Sciences & Department of Pathology and Microbiology - Atlantic Veterinary College Breadcrumb Home UPEI Human Resources Lecturer - Three-Year Term Position - Department of Biomedical Sciences & Department of Pathology and Microbiology - Atlantic Veterinary College Lecturer - Three-Year Term Position - Department of Biomedical Sciences & Department of Pathology and Microbiology - Atlantic Veterinary College Competition Number: 41A26 Position Type: Academic Opening Closing Date: Aug 7, 2026 Date of Posting: Jul 24, 2026 Department: Biomedical Sciences & Pathology and Microbiology Position: Lecturer Contract: Three-Year Term Salary: As per UPEI FA1 Collective Agreement Term: August 15, 2026 - August 15, 2029 The Atlantic Veterinary College (AVC) at the University of Prince Edward Island (UPEI) invites applications for a full-time contract faculty position at the rank of Lecturer . This will be a joint appointment with the Department of Biomedical Sciences and the Department of Pathology and Microbiology , and the contract is a 3-year term . Contract renewal will be based on performance, program requirements, and budgetary considerations. Responsibilities: The successful candidate will collaborate with discipline-specialist faculty to deliver laboratory-based teaching in veterinary microscopic anatomy, parasitology, bacteriology, and clinical pathology. The candidate will also participate in problem-based learning tutorials for veterinary students. Contribution to service and scholarly activity in relevant fields, including the scholarship of education, is expected. Other teaching and scholarly opportunities may be identified based on candidate interest and program needs. Qualifications: The successful candidate will: •    Have a DVM (or equivalent) degree •    Be strongly motivated to teach •    Have well-developed skills of collaboration, relationship-building, and communication •    Be a lifelong learner, eager to maintain skills and knowledge updated to contemporary standards in veterinary medicine and veterinary education Preference will be given to candidates with relevant clinical or diagnostic experience, teaching experience, or post-graduate training. Salary: The salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. UPEI faculty receive a comprehensive fringe benefits package with benefit details provided at the time of offer in accordance with the collective agreement. This appointment is subject to budgetary approval. AVC is located on the campus of UPEI in Charlottetown, Prince Edward Island (PEI). Nestled on the east coast of Canada, PEI is one of the world’s most beautiful islands and is home to sandy beaches, championship golf courses, bike and cross-country ski trails, and a vibrant arts community. Further details can be obtained at www.upei.ca/~avc and www.princeedwardisland.ca/en/about-pei . Application Instructions: Applicants should submit a letter of intent, a curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy and scholarly perspective, and contact information (including e-mail addresses) of 3 references. In the statement of teaching philosophy and scholarly perspective, candidates are encouraged to consider principles of Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion (EDI). Applications should be addressed to: Dr. Susan Dawson, Professor and Chair Department of Biomedical Sciences Atlantic Veterinary College University of Prince Edward Island 550 University Avenue Charlottetown PE C1A 4P3 Email: sdawson@upei.ca Phone: 902-566-0808 UPEI is committed to equity, diversity, inclusion, and reconciliation and believes in providing a positive learning and working environment where every person feels empowered to contribute. UPEI is committed to the principle of equity in employment and encourages applications from underrepresented groups, including women, Indigenous peoples, visible minorities, persons with disabilities, persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity, and others with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. In accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given priority. Closing date is August 7th , 2026; however, the competition will remain open until suitable candidates are identified. UPEI encourages all qualified applicants to apply for job openings; however, in keeping with the terms and provisions of the university’s various employment and collective agreements, first priority will be given to internal candidates. 550 University Ave, Charlottetown Prince Edward Island, Canada C1A 4P3 Quick Links Academic Calendar MyUPEI | Campus Login Bookstore Staff and Faculty Lookup Study Abroad Library Explore the Campus Crisis Centre Athletics and Recreation Moodle Research Faculties and Schools Conference Services Health and Wellness Sexual Violence Prevention and Response Office The University of Prince Edward Island recognizes and acknowledges our location in the unceded, traditional territory of the Mi’kmaq People of PEI. Connect with UPEI Copyright © 2026  University of Prince Edward Island. All Rights Reserved | Disclaimer | Privacy Policy | UPEI SAFE | Website Edits Our website uses cookies to provide the best browsing experience. By using this site or closing this message, you agree to our Disclaimer and Web Privacy Statement . Read Disclaimer OK No, thanks"
